 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 504779,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The sun, Venus, and Jupiter all line up on a given day. Venus orbits the sun once every 255 days. Jupiter orbits the sun every 4,330 days (we’ll ignore the decimal values of days for each orbit). How many days will it be until they line up again?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find the LCM of 255 and 4,330.</p>\n<p>Find the prime factorization of each number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"255 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 17\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4,330 = 2 \\times 5 \\times 433\"></span></p>\n<p>Make a table of each prime and the largest exponent for each prime.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prime</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>433</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exponent</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LCM is the product of each prime raised to the powers identified in the table.</p>\n<p>The LCM i <span data-math=\"2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 17 \\times 433 = 220,830\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The sun, Venus, and Jupiter will align in 220,830 days.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The sun, Venus, and Jupiter will line up again in 220,830 days."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
